---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
import TripteronWorkspaceStudy from "../../components/TripteronWorkspaceStudy.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  <article class="space-y-12">
    <header id="overview">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-5">Tripteron</h1>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700">I developed the kinematic model, path planner, and browser controls for a parallel robot at UCLA's Robotics and Mechanisms Laboratory. The software maps Cartesian targets to coordinated carriage motion and checks joint limits, rail travel, and modeled collisions.</p>
      <ProjectTags />
    </header>

    <figure>
      <img src="/media/tripteron/concept.png" alt="Concept rendering of two mirrored Tripteron platforms supporting a light" class="mx-auto w-full max-h-[426px] object-contain" width="939" height="1025" />
    </figure>

    <section id="kinematics" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Mechanism and calibration</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Four two-link chains support a translating platform. Each link is 140 mm long. Three carriage groups drive the mechanism: the upper pair shares carriage M; the lower chains use carriages L and R. Platform orientation is fixed in the model.</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Extracted hinge axes and linkage geometry from STEP assemblies using Python and OpenCascade.</li>
        <li>Registered the CAD frame to a measured calibration pose.</li>
        <li>Implemented target selection, path preview, and controller-state checks in a browser interface.</li>
      </ul>
      <div id="cad" class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 pt-4">
        <a href="/media/tripteron/1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="sm:col-span-2" aria-label="Open full Tripteron CAD assembly view">
          <img src="/media/tripteron/1.png" alt="Tripteron CAD assembly with three motors, linear rails, linkages, and moving platform" class="w-full h-auto" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <a href="/media/tripteron/2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open Tripteron CAD end view">
          <img src="/media/tripteron/2.png" alt="End view of the Tripteron linkage and platform" class="w-full aspect-[3/2] object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <a href="/media/tripteron/4.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open Tripteron CAD side view">
          <img src="/media/tripteron/4.png" alt="Side view of the Tripteron rails, carriage, and linkage" class="w-full aspect-[3/2] object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="motion-mapping" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Coordinates and motion mapping</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">The local frame has X to the robot's right, Y upward along the rails, and Z outward from the mounting plane. Position is measured from the physical calibration pose. Positive carriage travel is upward.</p>
      <table class="technical-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Platform translation and physical carriage motion</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Platform motion</th><th scope="col">Carriage response</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">+X: right</th><td>L moves down; R moves up; M remains stationary.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">+Y: up</th><td>All three carriages move up equally.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">+Z: outward</th><td>M moves up; L and R move down equally.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="equation" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Carriage displacement matrix">
        <math display="block" aria-label="Delta q M, L, R equals the CAD-derived matrix times delta X, Y, Z">
          <mrow>
            <mo>[</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Δq</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Δq</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Δq</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo>
            <mo>≈</mo>
            <mo>[</mo><mtable columnalign="right right right" columnspacing="0.8em">
              <mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.9271</mn></mtd></mtr>
              <mtr><mtd><mn>−1.3636</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>−0.9271</mn></mtd></mtr>
              <mtr><mtd><mn>1.3636</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>−0.9271</mn></mtd></mtr>
            </mtable><mo>]</mo>
            <mo>[</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>ΔX</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>ΔY</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>ΔZ</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo>
          </mrow>
        </math>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">CAD-derived displacement mapping; all displacements are in millimetres. q denotes physical carriage travel. Motor direction and command scale are applied separately.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="constraints" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Motion constraints</h2>
      <table class="technical-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Single-platform constraints</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Constraint</th><th scope="col">Effect on motion</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Joint reach</th><td>Compression floors and an extension cap limit folding and straightening on the selected linkage branch.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Rail travel</th><td>Each carriage must remain within its travel limits. Outward extension reduces the upper carriage's remaining upward travel.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Collision clearance</th><td>STEP distance checks cover three carriage-foot pairs. Belt and other contacts require additional modeling.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Path feasibility</th><td>Constraints must hold between targets, including interior minima in linkage span.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="path-planning" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Path planning</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Analytical linkage-span checks along straight segments.</li>
        <li>Conservative bounds and recursive subdivision for curved paths.</li>
        <li>Quintic path optimization using joint margins, carriage separation, length, and curvature.</li>
        <li>Checked segments sent to Klipper's shared motion queue for coordinated interpolation and look-ahead.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="paired-motion" class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="paired-workspace-heading">
      <h2 id="paired-workspace-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold">Paired-platform motion</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">The paired model treats the light as a rigid span between two opposed platforms at equal calibration heights. Robot B is rotated 180° about world Y, so its local X and Z directions oppose robot A's. Each platform translates without rotating; articulated attachments allow the light to tilt.</p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Let p₁ = (x₁, y₁, z₁) and p₂ = (x₂, y₂, z₂) be local attachment positions. In robot A's world frame:</p>
      <div class="equation paired-equations" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Paired attachment positions and rigid-length constraint">
        <p>A = (x₁, y₁, z₁)</p>
        <p>B = (−x₂, y₂, D₀ − z₂)</p>
        <p>‖B − A‖ = L</p>
        <p class="length-equation"><span>(x₁ + x₂)² + (y₂ − y₁)²</span> <span>+ (D₀ − z₁ − z₂)² = L²</span></p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">L is the fixed distance between attachments. D₀ is their separation at calibrated zero, not the mounting-plane spacing. The model places attachments at the platform origins.</p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">The same carriage mapping applies in each robot's local frame.</p>
      <table class="technical-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Translation and tilt of the paired light</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Light motion</th><th scope="col">Platform coordination</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Vertical translation</th><td>Both local Y coordinates change equally.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Lateral translation</th><td>Local X coordinates change by equal and opposite amounts.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Depth translation</th><td>One platform extends as the other retracts by the same amount.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Tilt</th><td>Differential endpoint motion changes the light direction while preserving L.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Both platforms must satisfy their joint, rail, and path constraints at the same time.</li>
        <li>The endpoint distance must remain constant throughout the trajectory.</li>
        <li>Attachment angular limits and robot/light swept-volume clearance need separate checks; they are excluded from the current workspace study.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="paired-study" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Paired workspace study</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">I built an offline simulator to evaluate shared reach. This study holds the light level and varies the initial outward extension of both platforms.</p>
      <TripteronWorkspaceStudy />
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">The largest sampled connected area was 172.25 cm² at Z = 65 mm, about 1.5% above the 75 mm case.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="testing" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Testing</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Hardware: motion direction, coordinated moves, startup, and return sequences.</li>
        <li>Software: inverse consistency, path constraints, stale controller state, and queue behavior.</li>
        <li>Position feedback: reconstructed from commands; independent pose measurement is planned for accuracy and repeatability tests.</li>
        <li>Paired operation: attachment loads, additional collisions, and synchronized hardware tests remain to be evaluated.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</ProjectLayout>

<style>
  [id] { scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
  .technical-table { width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; }
  .technical-table th, .technical-table td { padding: 0.8rem 0.65rem; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-border); overflow-wrap: break-word; line-height: 1.55; }
  .technical-table th:first-child { width: 29%; }
  .technical-table tbody th { font-weight: 500; }
  .technical-table td { color: var(--site-muted); }
  .equation { overflow-x: auto; padding: 1rem 0; color: var(--site-text); }
  .equation math { width: max-content; min-width: 100%; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .equation mtd { padding: 0.2em 0.3em; }
  .equation:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent-color); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .paired-equations { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.9; }
  .paired-equations p { width: max-content; min-width: 100%; margin: 0; }
  .paired-equations .length-equation { width: auto; }
  .length-equation span { display: inline-block; }
  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .technical-table { font-size: 0.875rem; }
    .technical-table th, .technical-table td { padding: 0.65rem 0.35rem; }
    .technical-table th:first-child { width: 34%; }
  }
</style>
